 "text": "Hey there, how are you holding up? Plan it ahead at a bench with a table cloth, or use a table cover. Fill boxes right after each person gets a piece, and keep food out of sight. Some do, many don't. Powerful hand held flashes are much more reliable. Keep food off the ground with a small table. Bugs can't bite through a thin film of liquid, they go for the bread you dip in. Fill those at the table, not right out in the open. A bug free bag helps several days.",
